          <strong>Universal Serial Bus (USB)</strong> is a serial cable commonly used to connect external devices to computers, laptops, tablets and smartphones. It can be plugged in or removed whilst the device is turned on (<strong>hot-swappable</strong>). Older serial and parallel cables required the computer to be turned off first.
